  "what": "The function `is_bpf_migration_disabled()` was rewritten from a simple `if (p->migration_disabled == 1) return p != current; else return p->migration_disabled;` into a nested conditional that first checks whether `CONFIG_PREEMPT_RCU` is enabled with `IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_PREEMPT_RCU)`. If `migration_disabled == 1` and PREEMPT_RCU is enabled, it returns `p != current`; otherwise it returns `true`. The surrounding comment block was also expanded and revised to explain that the BPF prolog only calls `migrate_disable()` when `CONFIG_PREEMPT_RCU` is enabled, and that `migration_disabled == 1` is ambiguous only in that configuration.",
